        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "There is [`FileType` event](https://neovim.io/doc/user/autocmd.html#FileType) which is usually a better choice for filetype-specific autocommands.\r\n\r\nSo something like this should work:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal openclose = function(data)\r\n  local enable = { nix = true, rust = true, lua = true }\r\n  local ft = vim.bo[data.buf].filetype\r\n  if enable[ft] then\r\n    MiniMap.open()\r\n  else\r\n    MiniMap.close()\r\n  end\r\nend\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('FileType', { callback = openclose, desc = \"Toggle 'mini.map' based on filetype\" })\r\n```",
