        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "In that case you can try to continue using `BufEnter` event but also add check for buffer's type. Something like this `if vim.bo.buftype ~= '' then return end`, i.e. only toggle map if entered \"normal\" buffer (and not terminal, scratch, quickfix, etc.). This should fix the issue with various temporary helper floating windows, because usually buffers there have 'buftype' equal to 'none'.",
